{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
  "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument this morning in Case 21-1195, Bittner versus United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Mr. Geyser, one of the contextual points that you raise and that I think has some force is that it's unusual for the government to impose draconian penalties on someone who is not willful, in other words, does not even perhaps know of the reporting obligation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Alexandru Bittner)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they're being penalized at an order of $10,000 a clip for every single account that was accidentally not reported."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Okay. And if we're in non-willful land, then we're in (5)(A), and it's the $10,000, and there's an opportunity, that's (a)(1), but then there's a reasonable cause exception, and this one got me a little tripped up, and I just want to make sure I understand your response because there the willful cause exception does reference the amount in accounts again. We go back to that. But the -- as I understand your position for -- and the American College helped me a little bit here, I think -- is that the -- that the balance in the account might become relevant as part of an affirmative defense that the taxpayer has to present if it wishes to avoid the non-willful violation on the basis of a reasonable excuse. Is -- is that -- have I got about right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They still get -- MR. GEYSER: -- the reasonable cause. JUSTICE GORSUCH: -- they still get zapped for the non-willful violation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let me just ask my concern. If you fail to file at all, are you eligible for the reasonable cause provision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GEYSER: I -- I agree, Your Honor, it's not a surprise, but I would say that a $10,000 penalty for most people for a paperwork error that they've done unwittingly, they haven't done -- they're not trying to hide anything, it's not accompanied by any substantive misconduct, a $10,000 hit for the average person who's unaware of the FBAR requirement is a pretty substantial hit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: So, if I have 20 accounts and I only keep records on one, I've only violated it once?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: In answer, following up on Justice Barrett's question, is there a temporal requirement for the reporting, failure to -- to -- I'm sorry, not reporting -- recordkeeping?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: One of the things that -- that seemed problematic to me is you cite 5314, but it doesn't mention accounts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: -- suppose someone reports multiple accounts, lists all that person's accounts but messes up the address as to each account. How many violations?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But if the government's telling taxpayers --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the critical guidance document here is the Internal Revenue Manual, which is the guidance document that IRS examiners apply in assessing penalties in these cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, before you move off that, the -- the March 2011 version of Letter 3709 says, \"For the failure to file TDF 90-22.1 due on or after June 30, 20\" -- \"2005, the penalty cannot exceed $10,000.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about criminal violations? Do you have the same reading?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district court rejected his reasonable cause -- his assertion of the reasonable cause defense. The Fifth Circuit affirmed that on de novo review."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No. Could you return once again to your understanding of the relationship between the reasonable cause requirement and ignorance of the law? Your first answer, when I asked that, was ignorance of the law is not reasonable cause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Am I right that you can get judicial review before you're forced to pay, unlike in some tax situations?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0003-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the form interacts with -- with -- with your understanding of the penalties. As I understand it, on the form, if -- if you have 25 or more bank accounts, and we're talking about in aggregate $10,000, not one bank account, in aggregate. But, if -- if -- if it's over 25, you -- you tick a box and you're done. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
      "evidence_id": "ev-97cc5e57ff49-0003-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 80,
        "start": 80
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is some basic information besides just checking the box, isn't there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1195",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "97cc5e57ff49878b629be55f2ed885bb808819236481742f11328c2a79631c48",
